\cf0 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony emerged from the garden onto the promenade. The polished black wall of the building confronted him like a cliff face, if that cliff face had etched and carved on it\'97and somehow holographically enhanced\'97a three-metre stylised depiction of a rose. As Tony approached, the rose appeared to change, from a near invisible carving in the wall, to a lurid fluorescent painting, to a coppery wire-frame. Tony squinted into the depths of the wall and thought perhaps he could see through it, as if it was very smoky glass, or into it, like a very precious black opal. As he came to stand before it, sunlight struck with galactic clarity and the rose became three-dimensional and alive. Perhaps it was the scent of the rose garden behind Tony\'97he reached out, expecting to feel the velvety texture of its petals. But all Tony felt was nothing, emptiness, thin air. He recoiled with shock.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Perhaps the jolt jogged Tony\'92s memory; he thought of Halo\'92s vid message and the strange card that appeared after on his tablet. He fumbled into his coat pocket, retrieved his device, and swiped and tapped until the card was again on his screen.\
